<title>NETHERLANDS: Philips restructures corporate HQ.</title>
<headline>Philips restructures corporate HQ.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics NV said on Tuesday it planned to restructure its corporate centre in Eindhoven and that a reduction in the number of jobs there was unavoidable.</p>
<p>A Philips spokesman said over 800 people were employed at the centre, covering financial, legal, fiscal, press office and other administrative posts.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the move was independent of Monday's profit warning, which also referred to accelerating planned actions for recovery.</p>
<p>Philips on Monday said a previously forecast improvement in second half operating profit was unlikely based on preliminary information from the third quarter, causing its shares to close over two percent lower.</p>
<p>&quot;This programme should ensure and enhance clear accountability at management level, eliminate excessive coordination, improve flexibility and reduce cost of organisation,&quot; a statement from Philips said.</p>
</text>
